	title 'Quickdraw Auxilary QDAux/MAIN'******************************************************************	 Copyright (C) 1986-1992*	 Apple Computer, Inc.*	 All Rights Reserved*********************************************************************************************************************************** Quickdraw Auxilary Version 3.2** Steven E. Glass* Bennet Marks* Art Cabral** Version 1.0    April 12, 1987** Version 2.0    May 8, 1987** Version 2.1    May 22, 1987   Steven Glass**   Fixed bug in origin handling in pictures and changed*   CallPutPic so it would not trash TEMP2 (a location relied*   upon by various	routines like the one that puts round*   rects into pictures.** Version 2.2    Jun 05, 1987   Steven Glass**   Fixed bug in copy pixels where right edge of image was often the*   wrong color when image was reduced by more than 2 : 1.	Problem was*   with fix ratio calculation of horizontal error term. Both the numerator*   and denominator	were 0 based values	rather than the 1 based values*   expected.** Version 2.3    **   Oct 14, 1987	Gary Phipps**   Fixed bug in picture drawing routines that handled the chextra opcode.**   18 Dec 87   Steven Glass**   Fixed bug in drawpicture that left fonts used in non-purgable*   state.**   20 Dec 87   Steven Glass**   Added SpecialRect, a routine to frame and fill a rectangle*   in a single call quickly and easily.**   18 Jan 88   Steven Glass**   Fixed bug in DrawPicture related to	pen size for*   pictures that are scaled.**   19 Jan 88   Steven Glass**   Fixed bug in UpdateStateRec related	to text drawing.*   When the grafport had no font id in	it, the fontid that	was*   constructed was	not correct.  The size part of the id was*   made from the style word in the font header rather than	the*   size word.**   18 Apr 88   Dan Oliver and Harry Yee   v2.4d2*   *   Some applications would load QDAux (i.e. Notes 'n' Files)  but never actually start it up.*   This caused problems for the control, window, and menu managers who*   made the call to SpecialRect.  Because QDAux is loaded but not started up, its*   WAP is incorrect (set to 0).  Therefore code was put in at the very start of *   SpecialRect to check, if the WAP is 0 then set a-reg to 1 (tool not found) set  *   carry and exit else go on.**   Fixed bug in SpecialRect where from QDStart the busy flag was being incremented but*   upon leaving SpecialRect it was never decremented. Fixed**   05 May 88   Harry Yee   v2.4d3**   Problem in DrawPicture (pics.asm) where _InstallFont is being called when *   Font Manager is not even loaded. (Happens in Finder when 'Show Clipboard'*   is selected after a picture has been copied to the clipboard.) Fixed it by*   just checking carry after InstallFont is called and cleaning up stack if *   an error did occurr and then going on.**   17 May 88	Steven Glass**   Fixed bug in SpecialRect relating to top and bottom lines not*   begin colored.  Also sped up drawing routines.**   Changed fix to busy flag by removing decrement and fixing*   BusyEC8 below.**   15 Jun 88	Harry Yee**   Prototype bit taken out of version number.($0204)** Version 2.5**   Bugs, fixed, version changed.  Docs in Projector.** Version 2.6**   19 Sep 88	Sue Dumont**   Added SeedFill and CalcMask**   15 May 89	Steven Glass**   Broke tool into 4 segments: main, pictures, stretch and*   seedfill.  This makes the main footprint in memory much*   smaller.**   Added dummy code that jml's into the real code through*   the jump tables.*   *   Brought part of PutPictStuff into this file so it would not*   force the load of the picture code unless a picture was*   being saved.** 31 May 89	Harry Yee** Change version number from $8206 to $0300.** 24-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Changed version number to $8303.  (See comments in other files.)** 27-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Changed version to $0303 for 5.0.4.** 10-Dec-90	Dave Lyons** Changed version to $8304 for 6.0.  (Checked in fix for DrawPicture* bombing on invalid picture opcodes.)** 4-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Made DrawPicture disable FastPort features (see pics.asm).** 10-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Added new call $0F12 GetSysIcon to centralize all those little* small icons for devices and folders and documents used in* Standard File, Find File, and Installer.  InsertPathMItems* will use this call, too.** 12-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Redefined flag bits for GetSysIcon so I can have a "misc"* category in addition to files and devices.  Added icons* for Desktop, Padlock, Up Arrow, Down Arrow, and Boxed* Down Arrow.** 14-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Moved the open-folder icon up one pixel so it looks okay in* menu items.** Widened the boxed-down-arrow icon so it looks more like the* regular down arrow icon.** Widened the Desktop icon so it's the same width as the folders* and disks.** 15-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Making the closed folder yellow.  Adding a CD-ROM icon.** 17-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Fixed up the little 3.5 Disk icon and added a new "gray 3.5"* icon to return for Device_ID $FFFF (used by InsertPathMItems* for offline volumes).** 19-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Added three calls from the DTS Libraries and Tools source:* PixelMap2Rgn, NewPort, and KillPort (by Eric Soldan).  Fiddled* with the stack-cleanup routines to work as tools and use ToStrip.** 19-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Added new call $1312 IBeamCursor, stolen from FakeModalDialog,* to set the cursor to an IBeam cursor.  There is only one* version now, but we may need a 320-mode version later.** 14-Feb-91 am	Dave Lyons** Changed name of GetOSIcon to GetSysIcon.* Changed IBeamCursor to use rCursor resource $07FF0001 instead* of hard-coding our own picture of it here.** 14-Feb-91 pm	Dave Lyons** Added WhooshRect call to animate zooming rectangles (stolen* from the Finder, code originally by Andy Stadler, later* modified by Dan Oliver and then Andy Nicholas).** 15-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** WhooshRect bit 30 now makes it *not* force the Window Manager* port.** 25-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Made NewPort/KillPort stuff conditional assembly, and conditioned* it out.  (It's more useful as sample code than part of the toolbox.)** 9-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Changed WhooshRect to return right away if either rectangle pointer* is NIL.  And now it calls SysBeep2($8040) for whoosh-open, $8041* for whoosh-closed.** Defined WhooshRect bit 29 = no sound.** 14-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** IBeamCursor uses  rCursor $07FF0001 for 640, $07FF0101 for 320.* Moved the GetSysIcon document icon one pixel to the left.* Removed gray shading from the regular 3.5 disk icon.* Fixing RAMDisk coloring so I can draw it at an even X coordinate.** 5-Apr-91	Dave Lyons** Changed PixelMap2Rgn so that it works okay if you include black* as one of the colors you want in your region.** Note: The boundsRect of the locInfo must not have negative*       coordinates, or it won't work right.** 23-Jun-91	Dave Lyons** In PixelMap2Rgn, covered additional rectangular-region case.* It was working okay if the region turned out to be rectangular* and the bottom matched the bottom of the bounds rectangle, but* if we hit the bottom of the region sooner, we didn't wind up* with a 10-byte region.** 26-Aug-91	Dave Lyons** Fix colors on GetSysIcon's AppleShare icon.  There are now* separate versions for 640/320, and the colors match the large* icons now used by Finder/EasyMount/AppleShare CP.** 29-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** Add a GetSysIcon icon for HyperMedia documents (file type $55).** 9-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** Put in real non-rectangular masks for the up-arrow and down-* arrow icons (in GetSysIcon).** 5-Feb-92	Dave Lyons** Version $0304 for 6.0 final.******************************************************************** BEGIN 6.0.1** 5-Mar-92	Dave Lyons** Version $8305 for 6.0.1d2.** Adding DrawStringWidth call.** 6-Mar-92	Dave Lyons** Saved 2 bytes in IBeamCursor (ORA #1 --> INC A).** 11-Mar-92	Dave Lyons** Added new GetSysIcon icons from Andy Nicholas for TXT, SRC, BAS,* archive, and BIN.** Implemented DrawStringWidth.** 12-Mar-92	Dave Lyons** Oops, got the left and right truncation codes backwards from* how I wanted them.** 3-Sep-92	Dave Lyons** Made GetSysIcon expandable by calling SendRequest.  If somebody* accepts the request, they get to provide the icon, overriding* what we would do. -- If this proves to be too slow, I'll take it* back out.** 16-Mar-93	Dave Lyons for 6.0.1d15** Added UseColorTable and RestoreColorTable.** 1-Apr-93	Steve Stephenson** Version $0305 for 6.0.1 (final)******************************************************************	blanks off	include 'all.macros'	include 'special.macros'	include 'E16.Memory'	include 'E16.Resources'DebugSymbols	equ 0NewPortKillPort	equ 0*** From E16.QuickDraw (for the NewPort/KillPort stuff); offset constants for GrafPortoportInfo	equ 0oportRect	equ 16	; PortRectoclipRgn	equ 24	; Clip Rgn. PointerovisRgn	equ 28	; Vis. Rgn. PointerobkPat	equ 32	; BackGround PatternopnLoc	equ 64	; Pen LocationopnSize	equ 68	; Pen SizeopnMode	equ 72	; Pen ModeopnPat	equ 74	; Pen PatternopnMask	equ 106	; Pen MaskopnVis	equ 114	; Pen VisableofontHandle	equ 116ofontID	equ 120	; Font IDofontFlags	equ 124	; FontFlagsotxSize	equ 126	; Text SizeotxFace	equ 128	; Text FaceotxMode	equ 130	; Text ModeospExtra	equ 132	; Fixed Point ValueochExtra	equ 136	; Fixed Point ValueofgColor	equ 140	; ForeGround ColorobgColor	equ 142	; BackGround ColoropicSave	equ 144	; PicSaveorgnSave	equ 148	; RgnSaveopolySave	equ 152	; PolySaveografProcs	equ 156oarcRot	equ 160	; ArcRotouserField	equ 162	; UserFieldosysField	equ 166	; SysField; offset constants for LocInfooportSCB	equ 0optrToPixImage	equ 2owidth	equ 6oboundsRect	equ 8*** From E16.Types; offset constants for Rectov1	equ 0oh1	equ 2ov2	equ 4oh2	equ 6; Equates from file	QDAUX.ASM** ToolNumber	equ 18QDAuxVersion	equ $0305	;1-Apr-93 SSQDAuxToolNum	equ 18QDToolNum	equ 4	include 'QDAuxEquates.asm'	;added 12-Jan-91 DAL	include '::qd:qdequates:core.globals1'	include '::qd:qdequates:core.globals2'	include '::qd:qdequates:region.equs'	include '::qd:qdequates:rect.equs'	include '::qd:qdequates:qd.data.asm'	include '::sys.equs.asm'***************************************************	Imports	         ***************************************************	Import BusyErr	Import BusyEC	Import EndCall	Import ErrOut	Import DisposeTB2	Import RestoreTextVectors	Import oEndCall	Import PSetTB2	Import PGetTB2Handle	Import SetupTextVectors	Import iStdPixels	Import iPicComment	Import iStdPutPic	Import iStdGetPic	Import iKillPicture	Import iDrawPicture	Import iClosePicture	Import iOpenPicture	Import iPutPictStuff	Import iStdComment	Import DrawIcon	Import CopyBits	Import SpecialRect***************************************************	Entries	         ***************************************************	Entry TheWatch320	Entry TheWatch640	Entry OrigStdPixels	Entry OrigPicComment	Entry OrigStdPutPic	Entry OrigStdGetPic	Entry OrigKillPicture	Entry OrigDrawPicture	Entry OrigClosePicture	Entry OrigOpenPicture	Entry OrigPutPictStuff	Entry OrigStdComment	Entry WaitCursor	Entry Reset	Entry Version	Entry QDAuxShutdown	Entry QDAuxStartup	Entry BootInit	Entry QDAuxStatus	title 'Quickdraw Auxilary pics/CALL.TABLE'TheCallTable	PROC EXPORT	import FakeSeedFill	import FakeCalcMask	import FakeCopybits	import GetSysIcon	import PixelMap2Rgn		;19-Jan-91 DAL	import NewPort		;19-Jan-91 DAL	import KillPort		;19-Jan-91 DAL	import WhooshRect		;14-Feb-91 DALTheBeginning	DC.L (TheEnd-TheBeginning)/4	DC.L BootInit-1		;$0112	DC.L QDAuxStartup-1		;$0212	DC.L QDAuxShutdown-1	;$0312	DC.L Version-1		;$0412	DC.L Reset-1		;$0512	DC.L QDAuxStatus-1		;$0612	DC.L Reset-1		;$0712	DC.L Reset-1		;$0812	DC.L FakeCopyBits-1		;$0912	DC.L WaitCursor-1		;$0A12	DC.L DrawIcon-1		;$0B12	DC.L SpecialRect-1		;$0C12 ; added permanently 3/31/88	DC.L FakeSeedFill-1		;$0D12	DC.L FakeCalcMask-1		;$0E12*** 6.0 ***	dc.l GetSysIcon-1		;$0F12 12-Jan-91 DAL (6.0)	dc.l JumpPixelMap2Rgn-1	;$1012 19-Jan-91 DAL (6.0)	dc.l Reset-1		;$1112	dc.l Reset-1		;$1212	dc.l IBeamCursor-1		;$1312 19-Jan-91 DAL (6.0)	dc.l WhooshRect-1		;$1412 14-Feb-91 DAL (6.0)*** 6.0.1 ***	dc.l DrawStringWidth-1	;$1512 5-Mar-92 DAL for 6.0.1	dc.l UseColorTable-1	;$1612 9-Nov-92 DAL for 6.0.1	dc.l RestoreColorTable-1	;$1712 9-Nov-92 DAL for 6.0.1TheEndJumpPixelMap2Rgn	jml PixelMap2Rgn	ENDP********************************************************************************************************************************************	title 'Quickdraw Auxilary pics/INIT.CALLS'InitCalls	PROC EXPORT	Export VersionVersion	lda #QDAuxVersion	Export QDAuxStatusQDAuxStatus	sta 7,s	brl Reset****************************************************************** QDAuxStartup** This routine saves all the vectors we	will clobber and then* clobbers them. It	also sets the WAP entry for this tool to the* same value used by QuickDraw.*****************************************************************	Export QDAuxStartupQDAuxStartup***	cmp #0	tay	;24-Sep-90 DAL	beq CanInitialize	brl GetOutCanInitialize		;	phd	; save direct;----------------------------------------------------;; Get QuickDraw's WAP and set our WAP to that value.;***	PushLong #0	; space for result	pha	;24-Sep-90 DAL	pha	;24-Sep-90 DAL	PushWord #0	; system	PushWord #QDToolNum	_GetWAP	pla	ply	tcd	; also set the direct reg	PushWord #0	; system	PushWord #QDAuxToolNum	phy	pha	_SetWAP;----------------------------------------------------;; Save the data bank and set it to bank	E0 where; the vectors are.	phb	; save data bank	pea $E0E0	; set to e0 to set vectors up	plb	plb;----------------------------------------------------;; Now, I save the vectors I am going to	replace.;	lda |StdComment+1	sta >OrigStdComment	lda |StdComment+2	sta >OrigStdComment+1	lda |PutPictStuff+1	sta >OrigPutPictStuff	lda |PutPictStuff+2	sta >OrigPutPictStuff+1	lda |OpenPicture+1	sta >OrigOpenPicture	lda |OpenPicture+2	sta >OrigOpenPicture+1	lda |ClosePicture+1	sta >OrigClosePicture	lda |ClosePicture+2	sta >OrigClosePicture+1	lda |DrawPicture+1	sta >OrigDrawPicture	lda |DrawPicture+2	sta >OrigDrawPicture+1	lda |KillPicture+1	sta >OrigKillPicture	lda |KillPicture+2	sta >OrigKillPicture+1	lda |StdGetPic+1	sta >OrigStdGetPic	lda |StdGetPic+2	sta >OrigStdGetPic+1	lda |StdPutPic+1	sta >OrigStdPutPic	lda |StdPutPic+2	sta >OrigStdPutPic+1	lda |PicComment+1	sta >OrigPicComment	lda |PicComment+2	sta >OrigPicComment+1	lda |StdPixels+1	sta >OrigStdPixels	lda |StdPixels+2	sta >OrigStdPixels+1;----------------------------------------------------;; Now put my calls in place	lda #<FakeStdComment	sta |StdComment+1	lda #>FakeStdComment	sta |StdComment+2	lda #<FakePutPictStuff	sta |PutPictStuff+1	lda #>FakePutPictStuff	sta |PutPictStuff+2	lda #<FakeOpenPicture	sta |OpenPicture+1	lda #>FakeOpenPicture	sta |OpenPicture+2	lda #<FakeClosePicture	sta |ClosePicture+1	lda #>FakeClosePicture	sta |ClosePicture+2	lda #<FakeDrawPicture	sta |DrawPicture+1	lda #>FakeDrawPicture	sta |DrawPicture+2	lda #<FakeKillPicture	sta |KillPicture+1	lda #>FakeKillPicture	sta |KillPicture+2	lda #<FakeStdGetPic	sta |StdGetPic+1	lda #>FakeStdGetPic	sta |StdGetPic+2	lda #<FakeStdPutPic	sta |StdPutPic+1	lda #>FakeStdPutPic	sta |StdPutPic+2	lda #<FakePicComment	sta |PicComment+1	lda #>FakePicComment	sta |PicComment+2	lda #<iStdPixels	sta |StdPixels+1	lda #>iStdPixels	sta |StdPixels+2	jsr SetupTextVectors	jsl PGetTB2Handle	; get the second text buffer	jsl PSetTB2	; size the second text buffer	plb	; restore data bank	pld	; restore dGetOut	Export BootInitBootInit	Export CoreBootInitCoreBootInit	Export ResetReset	ldy #0	brl oEndCall****************************************************************** QDAuxShutdown** This routine puts	the vectors back to	their orig state.* It also sets the WAP entry for this tool to 0*****************************************************************	Export QDAuxShutdownQDAuxShutdown	cmp #0	beq GetOut	phd	tcd;----------------------------------------------------;; Save the data bank and set it to bank	E0 where; the vectors are.	phb	; save data bank	pea $E0E0	; set to e0 to set vectors up	plb	plb;----------------------------------------------------;; Now, I put back the vectors I changed	earlier.;	lda >OrigStdComment	sta |StdComment+1	lda >OrigStdComment+1	sta |StdComment+2	lda >OrigPutPictStuff	sta |PutPictStuff+1	lda >OrigPutPictStuff+1	sta |PutPictStuff+2	lda >OrigOpenPicture	sta |OpenPicture+1	lda >OrigOpenPicture+1	sta |OpenPicture+2	lda >OrigClosePicture	sta |ClosePicture+1	lda >OrigClosePicture+1	sta |ClosePicture+2	lda >OrigDrawPicture	sta |DrawPicture+1	lda >OrigDrawPicture+1	sta |DrawPicture+2	lda >OrigKillPicture	sta |KillPicture+1	lda >OrigKillPicture+1	sta |KillPicture+2	lda >OrigStdGetPic	sta |StdGetPic+1	lda >OrigStdGetPic+1	sta |StdGetPic+2	lda >OrigStdPutPic	sta |StdPutPic+1	lda >OrigStdPutPic+1	sta |StdPutPic+2	lda >OrigPicComment	sta |PicComment+1	lda >OrigPicComment+1	sta |PicComment+2	lda >OrigStdPixels	sta |StdPixels+1	lda >OrigStdPixels+1	sta |StdPixels+2	phk	plb	jsr RestoreTextVectors	plb	PushWord #0	; system	PushWord #QDAuxToolNum	PushLong #0	_SetWAP	jsl DisposeTB2	pld	brl Reset	ENDP*****************************************************************Stuff	PROC EXPORT** This contains the commonly used ending routines.  They * set the y-reg and call the shared code in common.*** Inputs:*	x-reg has error code if it is an error routine** Outputs:*	y-reg has number of bytes on stack to be stripped** External Refs:	import ErrOut	import EndCall	import BusyEC	import BusyErr** Entry Points:	Export ErrOut0	Export EndCall0	Export BusyEC0	Export BusyErr0	Export ErrOut4	Export EndCall4	Export BusyEC4	Export BusyErr4	Export BusyErr8	Export BusyEC8*	longa on	; mode	longi on** Change History** 17 May 88	Steven Glass** BusyEC8 was jumping to EndCall instead of BusyEC.*****************************************************************;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Zero bytes on stack;ErrOut0	ldy #0	brl ErrOutEndCall0	ldy #0	brl EndCallBusyEC0	ldy #0	brl BusyECBusyErr0	ldy #0	brl BusyErr;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Four Bytes on stack;ErrOut4	ldy #4	brl ErrOutEndCall4	ldy #4	brl EndCallBusyEC4	ldy #4	brl BusyECBusyErr4	ldy #4	brl BusyErr;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Eight Bytes on Stack;BusyErr8	ldy #8	brl BusyErrBusyEC8	ldy #8	brl BusyEC	ENDPOrigVectors	PROC	Export OrigStdCommentOrigStdComment	DS.B 3	Export OrigPutPictStuffOrigPutPictStuff	DS.B 3	Export OrigOpenPictureOrigOpenPicture	DS.B 3	Export OrigClosePictureOrigClosePicture	DS.B 3	Export OrigDrawPictureOrigDrawPicture	DS.B 3	Export OrigKillPictureOrigKillPicture	DS.B 3	Export OrigStdGetPicOrigStdGetPic	DS.B 3	Export OrigStdPutPicOrigStdPutPic	DS.B 3	Export OrigPicCommentOrigPicComment	DS.B 3	Export OrigStdPixelsOrigStdPixels	DS.B 3	ENDP	title 'Quickdraw Auxilary QDAux/WaitCursor'**************************************************************** WaitCursor** This routine takes no inputs and makes the cursor a watch* cursor.***************************************************************WaitCursor	PROC EXPORT	PushWord #0	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	beq Mode320	PushLong #TheWatch640Join	_SetCursor	rtlMode320	PushLong #TheWatch320	bra Join	Export TheWatch640TheWatch640	DC.W 9,3	DC.B $03,$ff,$fc,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $03,$ff,$fc,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $3f,$00,$0f,$c0,$00,$00	DC.B $f0,$0f,$00,$f0,$00,$00	DC.B $f0,$ff,$00,$ff,$00,$00	DC.B $f0,$00,$00,$f0,$00,$00	DC.B $3f,$00,$0f,$c0,$00,$00	DC.B $03,$ff,$fc,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $03,$ff,$fc,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $03,$ff,$fc,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $03,$ff,$fc,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $3f,$ff,$ff,$c0,$00,$00	DC.B $ff,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00	DC.B $ff,$ff,$ff,$ff,$00,$00	DC.B $ff,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00	DC.B $3f,$ff,$ff,$c0,$00,$00	DC.B $03,$ff,$fc,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $03,$ff,$fc,$00,$00,$00	DC.W 0,0	Export TheWatch320TheWatch320	DC.W 11,4	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $0f,$00,$00,$0f,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $f0,$00,$f0,$00,$f0,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $f0,$ff,$f0,$00,$ff,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $f0,$00,$00,$00,$f0,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $0f,$00,$00,$0f,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $0f,$ff,$ff,$ff,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $ff,$ff,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $ff,$ff,$ff,$ff,$ff,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $ff,$ff,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $0f,$ff,$ff,$ff,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.B $00,$ff,$ff,$f0,$00,$00,$00,$00	DC.W 0,0	ENDP**************************************************************** $1312 IBeamCursor -- 19-Jan-91 DAL** This routine takes no inputs and makes the cursor an I-Beam* cursor.***************************************************************IBeamCursor	PROC EXPORT	pha	pha	;space for LoadResource	pea $8027	;rCursor***	pushlong #$07ff0001*** 14-Mar-91 DAL--use different resource for 320-mode	pea $07FF	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	eor #$0080	asl a;;;	ora #1	;A=$0101 for 320 mode, $0001 for 640 mode*** saved two bytes 6-Mar-92 DAL	inc a*** end 6-Mar-92	pha*** end of 14-Mar-91 DAL	_LoadResource	bcs @error	phd	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [3],y	tax	lda [3]	sta 3	stx 5	;dereferenced handle in place	pld	_SetCursor	rtl@error	plx	plx	rtl;	PushWord #0;	_GetMasterSCB;	pla;	and #$0080;	beq Mode320;;	PushLong #IBeamCursor640;Join	_SetCursor;;	rtl;;Mode320	PushLong #IBeamCursor320;	bra Join;;IBeamCursor320;IBeamCursor640	dc.b 9,0,3,0;	dc.b $00,$F0,$F0,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$0F,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$0F,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$0F,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$0F,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$0F,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$0F,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$0F,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$F0,$F0,$00,$00,$00;		;	dc.b $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00;	dc.b 4,0,6,0	ENDP**************************************************************** $1412 WhooshRect(flags:LONG,smallrectPtr,bigrectPtr)* Added 14-Feb-91 DAL** WhooshRect animates a zoom-rectangle effect.  I'm borrowing* the code from the Finder for this, at least for the first* version.** Flags: Bit 31: 1 = zoom out (small to big)*        Bit 30: 1 = draw in current port (not window mgr port)*        Bits 29-0: reserved (use 0)** If either rectangle pointer is NIL, the call does nothing.** If we actually do a visual zoom effect, we also call* SysBeep2 just before ($8040 = zoom open, $8041 = closed).***************************************************************WhooshRect	procname	jsl $e10064	;incbusy	phb	phk	plb	phd	tsc	tcd	@oldD	equ 1@oldB	equ 3@rtl	equ 4@bigrect	equ @rtl+6@smallrect	equ @bigrect+4@flags	equ @smallrect+4	lda <@bigRect+1	beq @nilRectangle	lda <@smallRect+1	beq @nilRectangle	ldy #6@copyRects	lda [<@bigRect],y	sta bigRect,y	lda [<@smallRect],y	sta smallRect,y	dey	dey	bpl @copyRects	pha	pha	_GetPort	ldx #$8040	;SysBeep2 zoom-open, default to silence	lda <@flags+2	and #$2000	;bit 29 = no sound (9-Mar-91 DAL)	bne @noSound	lda <@flags+2	bmi @thisSound	inx	;$8041 = zoom-closed, default to silence@thisSound	phx	_SysBeep2@noSound	ldy @flags+2	;bit 31 = zoom direction, bit 30=use current port	jsr ZoomRect	_SetPort@nilRectangle	pld	plb	ldx #0	;no error	ldy #12	;strip 12 bytes	jml $e10180	;ToBusyStrip;================================================; Zoom RECT.  By Andy Stadler.; Optimized by Dan Oliver;================================================;;  In: Y bit 15 set to zoom up, bit 14 set to use cur port;      smallRect = small rect  (both in global coordinates);      bigRect = big RECT.;;================================================ZoomRect	namerectY1	equ 0rectX1	equ 2rectY2	equ 4rectX2	equ 6	phd	tsc	sec	sbc #14		;space for temp1..temp4	tcs	tcd	jsr Zoom2	tsc	clc	adc #14	tcs	pld	rtstemp1	equ 1zoomtemp2	equ temp1+4temp3	equ zoomtemp2+4temp4	equ temp3+2Zoom2	tya		;Remember direction	and #$8000	pha	tya	and #$4000	bne @useCurPort	pha		;Space for result.	pha	_GetWMgrPort		;Use window manager's port.	_SetPort@useCurPort	pea 2		;width	pea 1		;height	_SetPenSize		pea 15		;Solid pen.	_SetSolidPenPat	pea 2		;XOR mode.	_SetPenMode;;; --- Setup step constants depending on	direction ----------------------;	pla	bne @zoomUp		lda #$9999		;_FixRatio(3,5)	sta <temp1	stz <temp1+2	lda #1		;Fract for going down (just in case).	sta <zoomtemp2+2	stz <zoomtemp2	bra copyRects	@zoomUp	lda #$AAAA		;_FixRatio(5,3)	sta <temp1	lda #1	sta <temp1+2	lda #$0BF4		;_FixRatio(3/5,10000)	sta <zoomtemp2	stz <zoomtemp2+2;	ldx #3;	ldy #5;	lda 1,s;	beq ok1;;	tya;	txy;	tax;;ok1	pha		;Space for result.;	pha;	phx		;Pass ratio.;	phy;	_FixRatio;	pla;	sta <temp1		;Factor;	pla;	sta <temp1+2;;	pla		;Going up or down?;	beq copyRects		;Ready if going down.;;; --- Zoom from	smallRect to bigRect -------------------;;	pha	;Space for result.;	pha;	pea $01D3	;Setup 3/5^numsteps = 0.0467;	pea $2710;	_FixRatio;	pla;	sta <zoomtemp2	;Fract.;	pla;	sta <zoomtemp2+2	;; --- Copy first rect into workrect1, and zero workrects 2 and 3. -------;copyrects	ldx #22@loop	stz workRect1,x	dex	dex	bpl @loop	lda #7		;7 steps	sta <temp3	pha	pea 0		;WaitFromTime	pea 0		;DelayAmount	_WaitUntil	pla		;NewTime	sta timeBetweenRects;; --- Loop, calculating and drawing --------------------------------;lop2	jsr blender		;Compute new RECT.			;just a thought, but if we wanted to be sneaky we could poll for VBL here and only draw when;we're vertically blanked instead of waiting down below				lda #workRect3		;Draw newest.	jsr frameRect	lda workrect1+rectX1	;Anything to erase yet?	ora workrect1+rectX2	beq skip1	jsr frameRect1		;Erase oldest.skip1			ldx #0		;workRect1 = workRect2@loop	lda workRect2,x		;workRect2 = workRect3	sta workRect1,x	inx	inx	cpx #16	bne @loop	pha		;Space for result.	pha	pei <temp1+2		;Bump interpolation value.	pei <temp1	pei <zoomtemp2+2	pei <zoomtemp2	_FixMul	pla	sta <zoomtemp2	pla	sta <zoomtemp2+2	pha	lda timeBetweenRects	pha	pea $10		;delayAmount in 16'ths of a tick	_WaitUntil	pla	sta timeBetweenRects		dec <temp3		;Loop counter.	bne lop2;; --- Done.  Clean up and quit.;	jsr frameRect1		;Erase all the RECTs.	lda #workRect2	jsr frameRect	_PenNormal	rts	timeBetweenRects	dc.w 0		;this isn't realy what it claims to be, but it			;gets the point across -- andy;; Frame a workRect.;frameRect1	lda #workRect1frameRect	pea workRect1>>16	pha	_FrameRect	rts; Blender;;  OUT:  workRect3 = blend from smallRect and bigRect.;Blender	ldx #rectX2lop200	stx <temp4		;hold rect index here	pha		;Space for final FixRound call.	pha		;Space for result.	pha	pei <zoomtemp2+2		;fract * big rect	pei <zoomtemp2	lda bigRect,x	pha	pea 0		;big rect is integer.0	_FixMul		;(leave 1st result on stack)	pha		;Space for result.	pha	lda #0		;(1-fract) * small rect	sec	sbc <zoomtemp2	tay	lda #1	sbc <zoomtemp2+2	pha	phy	ldx <temp4	lda smallRect,x	pha	pea 0		;small rect is integer.0	_FixMul	clc		;add the two results	lda 1,s	adc 5,s	sta 5,s	lda 3,s	adc 7,s	sta 7,s	pla		;(trash old result)	pla	_FixRound	pla		;result of rounding	ldx <temp4	sta workrect3,x	dex		;Next side.	dex	bpl lop200	rtsbigRect      	DS.B 8smallRect     	DS.B 8workRect1	DS.B 8	;1, 2, and 3 must be togetherworkRect2	DS.B 8workRect3	DS.B 8	ENDP*****************************************************************FakeStuff	PROC** These routines force the load of the dynamic segment containing* SeedFill and calcmask.*** Inputs:*	nothing is touched!** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:	import ForceTheLoad	import ForcePicLoad	import ForceCopyBitLoad	import SeedFill	import CalcMask	import iStdComment	import iPutPicStuff	import iOpenPicture	import iClosePicture	import iDrawPicture	import iKillPicture	import iStdGetPic	import iStdPutPic	import iPicComment	import iStdPixels** Entry Points:	entry FakeSeedFill	entry FakeCalcMask	entry FakeStdComment	entry FakePutPictStuff	entry FakeOpenPicture	entry FakeClosePicture	entry FakeDrawPicture	entry FakeKillPicture	entry FakeStdGetPic	entry FakeStdPutPic	entry FakePicComment	entry FakeCopyBits*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************FakeSeedFill	jml SeedFillFakeCalcMask	jml CalcMaskFakeStdComment	jml iStdCommentFakePutPictStuffiPutPictStuff	pha	; save the noun	ldy #o_PicSave	lda [Portref],y	sta Temp	iny	iny	lda [Portref],y	sta Temp+2	ora Temp	bne DoTheWorkDone		;	phx	ldx #512	lda <DirtyDPFlags,x	ora #NoPictRecord	sta <DirtyDPFlags,x	plx	pla	; return with noun still in a	clc	; and carry clear	RTLDoTheWork	jml SaveSomethingFakeOpenPicture	jml iOpenPictureFakeClosePicture	jml iClosePictureFakeDrawPicture	jml iDrawPictureFakeKillPicture	jml iKillPictureFakeStdGetPic	jml iStdGetPicFakeStdPutPic;	jsl ForcePicLoad	jml iStdPutPicFakePicComment	jml iPicCommentFakeCopyBits	jml CopyBits	ENDP****************************************************************** QDStart** This is a local routine that increments the busy flag, saves* the current direct register on the stack and transfers* the a register to	the D register.** This is meant to be called at the start of any QD entry point* that requires zero page and the busy flag to be incremented.** In Doing this we trash the X-Register.  Hopefully this will* not cause anyone any problems.** We do know that A	and Y must be untouched.  Y for PortWord* and PortLong.  A for cursor routines that add $100 to A*****************************************************************QDStart	PROC EXPORT	jsl IncBusyFlg	phd	; push d on stack	tcd	; set d	lda 3,s	; getorig rts	pha	; put on stack	lda 3,s	; move orig d to on	top of rts	sta 5,s	pla	; pull rts off stack	sta 1,s	; put over orig d	tdc	; get QD D back in a	rts	; done	ENDP************************************************************************************* GetSysIcon -- new call 10-Jan-91 Dave Lyons** Description:** Inputs:** $0F12 GetSysIcon(flags: integer; value: integer; auxtype: long): IconPtr;** Flags bit 1-0:  00=get a File icon; 01=get a device icon;*                 10=get a misc icon; 11=invalid value*       bit 2:    0=use closed folders; 1=use open folders** Value: Depends on Flags.*        File: GS/OS File Type.*        Device: GS/OS Device_ID.*        Misc:*          0=Desktop icon*          1=padlock icon*          2=up arrow*          3=down arrow*          4=boxed down arrow** Auxtype:  For Files, pass auxiliary type.  For Devices and Misc, pass 0.************************************************************************************GetSysIcon	proc exportrtl1	equ 1rtl2	equ rtl1+3auxtype	equ rtl2+3value	equ auxtype+4flags	equ value+2IconPtr	equ flags+2*** added 3-Sep-92 DAL -- Try calling SendRequest to let folks customize us	tsc	;get a copy of teh stack pointer	pea $1201	;systemSaysGetSysIcon	pea $8000	;how=sendToAll+stopAfterOne	ldx #0	phx	phx	;target=nil	phx	;high word of input pointer	clc	adc #auxtype	pha	;low word of input pointer (point at stk parms)	pushlong #iconReqDataOut	_SendRequest	bcs @oldWay	lda >iconReqDataOut+2  ;low word of result	tay	lda >iconReqDataOut+4	brl @returnAY@oldWay*** end 3-Sep-92*** added 14-Mar-91 DAL: check 320/640 mode, keep result in X	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	tax*** end of 14-Mar-91 DAL	lda value,s	tay	;Value paramter in Y	lda flags,s	and #3	;low 2 bits = icon type	beq @doFile	;00=file	dec a	beq @doDevice	;01=device	dec a	beq @doMisc0	;10=misc@outOfRange	ldx #badGetSysIconInput	brl @error@doMisc0	brl @doMisc* Get a File icon@doFile	cpy #$000f	;Is it a Folder?	beq @isFolder;	cpy #$00ff	;Is it a SYS file?;	beq @isApplication;	cpy #$00B3	;Is it a S16 file?;	beq @isApplication;;*** added 29-Sep-91 -- special icon for HyperMedia documents (file type $55);	cpy #$0055;	bne @notStack;;	lda #^StackIcon;	ldy #StackIcon;	bra @returnAY0;@notStack;*** end 29-Sep-91 DAL;;	lda #^DocumentIcon;	ldy #DocumentIcon;	bra @returnAY0;;@isApplication	lda #^ApplicationIcon;	ldy #ApplicationIcon;	bra @returnAY0*** added 11-Mar-92 DAL -- make filetype check table driven	tya	;filetype in A	txy	;640 flag in Y	ldx #endFiletypes-Filetypes-2@search	cmp >Filetypes,x	beq @foundIt	dex	dex	bne @search@foundIt	tya	bne @640	lda >fileIcons320,x	bra @1@640	lda >fileIcons640,x@1	tay	lda #DocumentIcon>>16	bra @returnAY0*** end 11-Mar-92@isFolder	lda flags,s	;check bit 2 = Open/Closed folder icons	and #4	bne @isOpenFolder	txy	beq @isFolder320	lda #^FolderIcon	ldy #FolderIcon	bra @returnAY@isFolder320	lda #^FolderIcon320	ldy #FolderIcon320	bra @returnAY@isOpenFolder	txy	beq @isOpenFolder320	lda #^OpenFolderIcon	ldy #OpenFolderIcon	bra @returnAY@isOpenFolder320	lda #^OpenFolderIcon320	ldy #OpenFolderIcon320@returnAY0	bra @returnAY* Get a Device icon@doDevice	tya	;get Value in A	cmp #$ffff	;offline device?	beq @offline	cmp #EndOfTable-DevicePicNum	bcc @goodDevice	lda #3	;use same icon as Apple 3.5 drive, at least for now@goodDevice	phx	;15-Mar-91 DAL	tax	lda >DevicePicNum,x	plx	;15-Mar-91 DAL	and #$00ff	cmp #$00ff	bne @goodIcon	lda #5	;index to Null Icon	bra @goodIcon@offline	lda #7@goodIcon	txy	bne @goodIcon640	asl a	asl a	tax	lda >DeviceIconTable320,x	tay	lda >DeviceIconTable320+2,x	bra @returnAY@goodIcon640	asl a	asl a	tax	lda >DeviceIconTable,x	tay	lda >DeviceIconTable+2,x	bra @returnAY*** return a Miscellaneous icon@doMisc	tya	asl a	asl a	tax	cpx #MiscTableEnd-MiscIconTable	bcs @outOfRange0	lda >MiscIconTable,x	tay	lda >MiscIconTable+2,x	;fall into @returnAY@returnAY	sta IconPtr+2,s	tya	sta IconPtr,s@leave	ldx #0	;no error@error	ldy #8	jml $e10184	;ToStrip@outOfRange0	brl @outOfRange*** added 3-Sep-92 DALiconReqDataOut	dc.w 0	;space for recvCount	dc.l 0	;space for result	dc.l 0	;space for expansion*** end 3-Sep-92*** added 11-Mar-92 DALFiletypes	dc.w 0	;catch-all	dc.w $0004	;text	dc.w $0006	;binary	dc.w $0055	;stack	dc.w $00b0	;src	dc.w $00b3	;GS/OS application	dc.w $00e0	;archive	dc.w $00fc	;Applesoft	dc.w $00ff	;P8 applicationendFiletypesfileIcons320	dc.w DocumentIcon	dc.w textIcon	dc.w binIcon	dc.w stackIcon	dc.w srcIcon	dc.w ApplicationIcon	dc.w archiveIcon	dc.w basIcon	dc.w ApplicationIconfileIcons640	dc.w DocumentIcon	dc.w textIcon	dc.w binIcon	dc.w stackIcon	dc.w srcIcon	dc.w ApplicationIcon	dc.w archiveIcon	dc.w basIcon	dc.w ApplicationIcon*** end 11-Mar-92DevicePicNum	dc.b  $00	;dev_id 0 = DiskIcon5.25	dc.b  $02	;dev_id 1 = Profile 5MB	dc.b  $02	;dev_id 2 = Profile 10MB	dc.b  $01	;dev_id 3 = Apple 3.5	dc.b  $02	;dev_id 4 = SCSI Generic	dc.b  $02	;dev_id 5 = SCSI hard disk	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id 6 = SCSI Tape Drive	dc.b  $06	;dev_id 7 = SCSI CD-ROM (was $02 15-Jan-91 DAL)	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id 8 = SCSI Printer	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id 9 = Serial Modem	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id A = Console Driver	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id B = Serial Printer	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id C = Serial LaserWriter	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id D = AppleTalk LaserWriter	dc.b  $04	;dev_id E = RAM Disk	dc.b  $04	;dev_id F = ROM Disk	dc.b  $03	;dev_id 10 = File Server	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id 11 = (reserved)	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id 12 = Apple Desktop Busª	dc.b  $02	;dev_id 13 = Hard Disk (generic)	dc.b  $01	;dev_id 14 = Floppy Disk (generic)	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id 15 = Tape Drive (generic)	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id 16 = Character Device Driver (generic)	dc.b  $01	;dev_id 17 = MFM-encoded disk drive	dc.b  $03	;dev_id 18 = AppleTalk network (generic)	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id 19 = Sequential Access Device	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id 1A = SCSI Scanner	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id 1B = Other Scanner	dc.b  $FF	;dev_id 1C = LaserWriter SC	dc.b  $03	;dev_id 1D = AppleTalk Main Driver	dc.b  $03	;dev_id 1E = AppleTalk File Service driver	dc.b  $03	;dev_id 1F = AppleTalk RPM Driver	dc.b  $05	;dev_id 20 = Unassigned? --> Null icon EndofTable; the above numbers index into this table:DeviceIconTable	dc.l DiskIcon5_25		; 0 = 5.25 disk icon	dc.l DiskIcon3_5		; 1 = 3.5 disk icon	dc.l HDiskIcon		; 2 = Hard disk icon	dc.l AppleShareIcon		; 3 = Apple share	dc.l RamIcon		; 4 = RAM/ROM Disk	dc.l NullIcon		; 5 = Special null icon	dc.l CDROMIcon		; 6 = CD-ROM icon	dc.l OfflineDisk		; 7 = offline disk (gray 3.5)DeviceIconTable320	dc.l DiskIcon5_25_320	; 0 = 5.25 disk icon	dc.l DiskIcon3_5		; 1 = 3.5 disk icon	dc.l HDiskIcon320		; 2 = H